  {"id":"rhe-009","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Rhetoric and text analysis","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is a hasty generalisation?","svar":["Drawing a broad conclusion from too little evidence","A conclusion based on solid statistical evidence","A conclusion reached slowly over time","A type of rhetorical question"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"rhe-010","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Rhetoric and text analysis","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is a red herring in argumentation?","svar":["An irrelevant point introduced to distract from the real issue","The main argument of a text","A summary of the opposing view","A type of statistical evidence"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"rhe-011","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Rhetoric and text analysis","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is an ad hominem argument?","svar":["Attacking the person making an argument rather than the argument itself","A logical, evidence-based argument","An appeal to authority","A rhetorical question"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"rhe-012","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Rhetoric and text analysis","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is the purpose of a topic sentence?","svar":["It introduces the main idea of a paragraph, usually placed at the beginning","It always concludes the paragraph","It is always a question","It lists the sources used"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"rhe-013","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Rhetoric and text analysis","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is the difference between denotation and connotation?","svar":["Denotation is a word's literal, dictionary meaning; connotation is the associated feelings or ideas it carries","There is no difference","Denotation refers only to emotional meaning","Connotation refers only to literal meaning"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"rhe-014","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Rhetoric and text analysis","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is a euphemism?","svar":["A mild or indirect expression substituted for a harsh or blunt one, e.g. 'passed away' for 'died'","An exaggeration for effect","A direct insult","A type of rhyme"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"rhe-015","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Rhetoric and text analysis","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is understatement?","svar":["Deliberately presenting something as less significant than it is, often for ironic or humorous effect","An exaggeration for effect","A direct factual statement","A rhetorical question"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"rhe-016","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Rhetoric and text analysis","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is alliteration?","svar":["The repetition of the same initial consonant sound in nearby words, e.g. 'wild and windy'","A rhyme at the end of two lines","A repeated word at the end of sentences","A pause in speech"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"rhe-017","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Rhetoric and text analysis","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is an anaphora (repetition)?","svar":["The repetition of a word or phrase at the beginning of successive clauses or sentences","A rhyme scheme","A single repeated sound","A metaphor"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"rhe-018","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Rhetoric and text analysis","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is the tone of a text?","svar":["The author's attitude towards the subject or audience, conveyed through word choice and style","The literal meaning of the text","The text's length","The text's genre only"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"lan-001","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Language and language use","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is Received Pronunciation (RP)?","svar":["A prestige accent of British English, historically associated with the upper class and traditional BBC broadcasting, not tied to a specific region","The official language of the UK government only","A dialect spoken only in London","A form of American English"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"lan-002","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Language and language use","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is African American Vernacular English (AAVE)?","svar":["A dialect of English spoken by many African Americans, with its own grammar, vocabulary, and pronunciation patterns","An official government language","A form of British English","A type of slang used only online"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"lan-003","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Language and language use","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is a pidgin language?","svar":["A simplified language that develops as a means of communication between groups without a common language, typically with no native speakers","A native language of a small country","A dialect of English","A formal, literary style"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"lan-004","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Language and language use","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is a creole language?","svar":["A pidgin that has become the native language of a community, developing a fuller grammar and vocabulary","The same as a pidgin","A formal written style","An extinct language"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"lan-005","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Language and language use","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is English as a lingua franca?","svar":["The use of English as a common means of communication between speakers of different native languages","English spoken only by native speakers","A dialect of English spoken in Africa","A form of pidgin English"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"lan-006","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Language and language use","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is code-switching?","svar":["Switching between two languages or language varieties, often within the same conversation","Speaking very quickly","A type of formal writing","A spelling error"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"lan-007","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Language and language use","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is a loanword?","svar":["A word borrowed from another language and adopted into English, e.g. 'kindergarten' from German","A newly invented word","A word used only in slang","A grammatically incorrect word"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"lan-008","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Language and language use","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is the difference between British and American spelling, e.g. 'colour' vs 'color'?","svar":["British spelling often uses '-our' and follows older French-influenced patterns; American spelling was simplified, partly due to Noah Webster's reforms","There is no real difference between them","American spelling is older than British spelling","British spelling was simplified more than American"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"lan-009","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Language and language use","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is slang?","svar":["Very informal language, often specific to a particular group or time period, e.g. 'lit' or 'cool'","Formal, academic language","A regional dialect","A grammatical error"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"lan-010","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Language and language use","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is register in language use?","svar":["The level of formality or style used in language, appropriate to the situation, audience, and purpose","A grammatical rule","A dialect","A type of punctuation"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"lan-011","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Language and language use","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is a false friend in language learning?","svar":["A word in another language that looks or sounds similar to a word in your own language but has a different meaning, causing confusion","A word that is spelled the same in both languages with the same meaning","A word borrowed directly with no change in meaning","A slang term"],"forklaring":""},
  {"id":"lan-012","emne":"Engelsk","omraade":"Language and language use","type":"Begreb","format":"mc","spoergsmaal":"What is World Englishes as a field of study?","svar":["The study of how English varies and is used differently across different countries and cultures worldwide","The study of Old English only","A dictionary of English words","A grammar textbook"],"forklaring":""}
